{"schema":3,"source_digest":"04c06a1defdbdef36afcdb14d3bc596261c74eabc4561fff8d8f80f604472a63","dependencies":[],"processor_digest":"05407ea0b9fb79a4fb824e492c01e0ff56cb871c7ff102d6a368e95af20aa6f4","result":{"html":"<html><head></head><body><h1 id=\"from-source\">From source</h1>\n<p>Build <code>sessiond</code>, <code>sessionctl</code>, and the PAM module in release mode:</p>\n<html><head></head><body><pre class=\"highlight\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span style=\"color:rgb(97,175,239);\">cargo</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">build</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-p</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">sessiond</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-p</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">sessionctl</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-p</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">pam</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">--release</span><br></code></pre></body></html>\n<p>Install the binaries and PAM module:</p>\n<html><head></head><body><pre class=\"highlight\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span style=\"color:rgb(97,175,239);\">install</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-Dm755</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">target/release/sessiond</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">/usr/local/bin/sessiond</span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(97,175,239);\">install</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-Dm755</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">target/release/sessionctl</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">/usr/local/bin/sessionctl</span><br><span style=\"color:rgb(97,175,239);\">install</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-Dm755</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">target/release/libpam.so</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">/usr/lib/security/pam_sessiond.so</span><br></code></pre></body></html>\n<p>The <code>consolekit</code> feature enables the ConsoleKit compatibility layer. Include it\nwhen building if you need that support:</p>\n<html><head></head><body><pre class=\"highlight\"><code class=\"language-bash\"><span style=\"color:rgb(97,175,239);\">cargo</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">build</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">-p</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">sessiond</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">--release</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">--features</span>&nbsp;<span style=\"color:rgb(232,102,113);\">consolekit</span><br></code></pre></body></html>\n</body></html>","headers":[{"text":"From source","level":1,"id":"from-source"}],"title":"From source","included_files":[]},"frontmatter":null}